#!/bin/sh
# Wishlists, the Trading Hall and Auctions (Nathan, 2026-10-01). Desktop first; phones after approval.
cd /c/Users/vaugh/discord-design
RULES="Use the same colors, fonts and components as the existing screens in this file (the Community screen with its tabs, the 5-item dock, the top bar). Sample member names only. No explanatory subtitles or helper sentences under labels. No scrolling: everything fits one 1280 x 720 window; long lists use the existing pager (< 1 of 4 >)."
run() { echo "== $2"; pen --in "design/$1" --out "design/$2.pen" --prompt "$3 $RULES" --export "design/$2.png" --export-scale 2 2>&1 | sed 's/\x1b\[[0-9;]*m//g' | tail -2; }
run 16-community.pen 26-hall-a "Nathan's words: I'd like players to be able to set Wishlist cards on their profile (up to 5) that the community can see. All of these wishlists need to be organized by person into a trading hall / looking for hall where people can go in generally and see what others are searching for and can offer up trades for cards that way as well. Make 3 desktop frames, 1280 x 720, side by side, titled: 1) the member profile with its Wishlist section (up to 5 entries; each entry is a card and a rarity) and an edit state where the member picks a card and a rarity for a slot. 2) The Trading Hall as a new tab of the Community screen (beside Trades and Boons & Pranks): one row per member with their wishlist cards, and an Offer button on a card that I own. 3) The offer from the Hall: it uses the existing two-step trade (I offer the card they want, they pick one of my cards of the same rarity, then I accept)."
run 26-hall-a.pen 26-hall-b "Nathan's words: an auction where multiple people can offer up cards (as many as they want, different tiers) and compete. I can pick and choose between offers or reject them all. The auction is also available for Gold cards, which cannot normally be traded; for Gold cards only Full Arts, Promos or Event cards can be offered as bids. When someone puts up an auction, a notice is sent in Discord with a graphic, the card art, and what the person is looking for as a minimum; as people bid, that graphic updates, and the time left to bid is on it. Decided rules: the minimum is a rarity and a count (for example 2 Secret Rare) and the bids that meet it are marked; one active auction per member; one bid holds up to 5 cards; a bid on a non-Gold card cannot hold Gold cards; the auction runs 3 days, then every bid returns; bid cards are held while the bid is open; the Discord notice shows the bid count and a summary of the best bid (its cards and rarities, no names) and a live countdown, with the Open Lion Pride TCG button. Make 4 frames side by side, titled: 1) the Auctions tab of the Trading Hall (a grid of live auctions: card art, the minimum, the bid count, the time left; a Start auction button). 2) Start an auction: pick my card, set the minimum. 3) One auction as its seller sees it: the card, the minimum, the time left, the list of bids (each bid as its cards, a Meets minimum mark), Accept on each bid and Reject all; and the same auction as a bidder sees it with Place bid (pick up to 5 of my cards). 4) The Discord notice: the bot post in a Discord channel with the graphic (card art, minimum, bid count, best bid summary, time left) and the Open Lion Pride TCG button."
echo ALL-DONE
